    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38067" root="لوب" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُوبٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَوَائِبُ</span></b>  Camels, or palm-trees,
<i>thirsty; far from water.</i> (K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَكْتُهَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى الحَوْضِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَوَائِبَ</span></b>  <i>I left them</i> (the camels)
<i>going round about the tank,</i> or <i>cistern, unable to
get at the water, on account of the crowding,</i>
or <i>pressing.</i> (As, S.) [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوائب</span> is pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَائِبَةٌ</span>.]
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُوبٌ</span> <i>A piece of meat that turns round in
the cooking-pot.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُوبٌ</span> <i>Bees:</i> (K:)
accord. to some, originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُوبٌ</span>. (MF.) In
some copies of the K, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نخل</span> is erroneously put
for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نحل</span>. (TA.)

